Author: Stephan Renatus <stephan.renatus@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 22 10:37:58 2026 +0200

    topdown: start the partial-eval test server on first use
    
    testserver was a package-level var, so httptest.NewServer ran in init and every
    run of this package bound a port -- 'go test -bench' included, which needs no
    server at all. One test asks for it, TestTopDownPartialEval, and only for its
    URL.
    
    sync.OnceValue defers that to the first caller. Where a port cannot be bound the
    package's benchmarks now run instead of the binary dying before main.
    
    Signed-off-by: Stephan Renatus <stephan.renatus@gmail.com>

